From: b70-notes <b70-notes@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:09:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SYCL: Inkling 2 node-group fusions (clip, MoE router,
 SITU + expert scale, expert combine, mix, control, conv tail)

inkling-fuse.cpp matches the exact op chains of inkling2.cpp / build_moe_ffn, checks that no intermediate is
read outside the group and that the output does not overlap an input (ggml-alloc in-place reuse), and runs each
group as one or two kernels. GGML_SYCL_IFUSE=<mask> selects them (default all). The expert combine is limited
to <= 8 tokens: with more it hangs the device (not understood yet).
Decode graph 7609 -> ~3350 launches; NVFP4-Q8_0 tg64 37.5 -> 47.5, pp512 380 -> 542 (FA on).
KLD -ub 1 per fusion within +-0.0009 of the 0.0047 baseline (SITU bit-exact).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: otaliptus <56600661+otaliptus@users.noreply.github.com>
